{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Bayesian Last Layer + BoTorch\n","\n","This notebook uses a deterministic neural feature extractor and a Bayesian linear output layer. It is **not a full BNN**. The benefit is a much cheaper posterior update that can still support sequential optimization.\n","\n","```text\n","experiments → deterministic feature network → φ(x) → Bayesian linear layer → posterior weight samples → BoTorch qLogEI\n","```\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import numpy as np, matplotlib.pyplot as plt, torch, torch.nn as nn\n","from botorch.models.ensemble import EnsembleModel\n","from botorch.acquisition.logei import qLogExpectedImprovement\n","from botorch.optim import optimize_acqf\n","torch.manual_seed(42); np.random.seed(42); torch.set_default_dtype(torch.double)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Synthetic expensive process\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def black_box(X):\n","    x1,x2=X[...,0],X[...,1]\n","    p1=1.30*torch.exp(-22*((x1-.72)**2+(x2-.30)**2)); p2=.75*torch.exp(-35*((x1-.28)**2+(x2-.78)**2))\n","    return p1+p2+.12*torch.sin(8*x1)*torch.cos(7*x2)-.10*(x1-x2)**2\n","bounds=torch.tensor([[0.,0.],[1.,1.]])\n","sobol=torch.quasirandom.SobolEngine(2,scramble=True,seed=42); train_X=sobol.draw(16); train_Y=black_box(train_X).unsqueeze(-1)\n","print('Initial best score:',float(train_Y.max()))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Deterministic feature extractor\n","\n","Only the final Bayesian linear layer will represent parameter uncertainty.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["class FeatureNet(nn.Module):\n","    def __init__(self,d=2,h1=32,h2=16):\n","        super().__init__(); self.backbone=nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d,h1),nn.Tanh(),nn.Linear(h1,h2),nn.Tanh()); self.head=nn.Linear(h2,1)\n","    def features(self,X): return self.backbone(X)\n","    def forward(self,X): return self.head(self.features(X))\n","\n","def fit_net(X,Y,steps=1200):\n","    net=FeatureNet(X.shape[-1]); opt=torch.optim.Adam(net.parameters(),lr=.01); ym=Y.mean(); ys=Y.std().clamp_min(1e-6); Yz=(Y-ym)/ys\n","    for _ in range(steps):\n","        opt.zero_grad(); loss=((net(X)-Yz)**2).mean(); loss.backward(); opt.step()\n","    return net,ym.detach(),ys.detach()\n","net,y_mean,y_std=fit_net(train_X,train_Y)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Closed-form Bayesian linear posterior\n","\n","With augmented features \(\\tilde\\phi(x)=[1,\\phi(x)]\),\n","\n","\\[f(x)=\\tilde\\phi(x)^T\\beta,\\qquad \\beta\\sim N(0,\\alpha^{-1}I).\n","\n","Under Gaussian noise with precision \(\\tau\):\n","\n","\\[\\Sigma=(\\alpha I+\\tau\\Phi^T\\Phi)^{-1},\\qquad m=\\tau\\Sigma\\Phi^Ty.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def design(net,X):\n","    phi=net.features(X); return torch.cat([torch.ones(*phi.shape[:-1],1,dtype=phi.dtype),phi],-1)\n","def fit_bll(net,X,Y,ym,ys,alpha=1.0):\n","    Yz=((Y-ym)/ys).squeeze(-1)\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        Phi=design(net,X); resid=net(X).squeeze(-1)-Yz; noise_var=resid.pow(2).mean().clamp_min(2e-3); tau=1/noise_var; I=torch.eye(Phi.shape[-1])\n","        Sigma=torch.linalg.inv(alpha*I+tau*Phi.T@Phi); m=tau*Sigma@Phi.T@Yz\n","    return m,Sigma,noise_var\n","m,Sigma,noise_var=fit_bll(net,train_X,train_Y,y_mean,y_std); posterior=torch.distributions.MultivariateNormal(m,covariance_matrix=Sigma); beta_samples=posterior.rsample((256,))\n","print('Bayesian last-layer dimension:',m.numel())\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. BoTorch ensemble wrapper\n","\n","The same posterior weight sample is used across all candidate points, so each sample behaves like one function realization. The deterministic backbone remains differentiable with respect to the input.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["class BLLEnsemble(EnsembleModel):\n","    _num_outputs=1\n","    def __init__(self,net,beta,ym,ys):\n","        super().__init__(); self.net=net; self.register_buffer('beta',beta); self.register_buffer('ym',ym.reshape(())); self.register_buffer('ys',ys.reshape(()))\n","        for p in self.net.parameters(): p.requires_grad_(False)\n","    def forward(self,X):\n","        Phi=design(self.net,X); z=torch.einsum('...qp,sp->...sq',Phi,self.beta); return (z*self.ys+self.ym).unsqueeze(-1)\n","model=BLLEnsemble(net,beta_samples,y_mean,y_std)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. qLogExpectedImprovement\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["acq=qLogExpectedImprovement(model=model,best_f=train_Y.max()); candidate,value=optimize_acqf(acq_function=acq,bounds=bounds,q=1,num_restarts=10,raw_samples=128)\n","print('Suggested setting:',candidate.detach().numpy().round(4)); print('True synthetic value:',float(black_box(candidate)))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Practical interpretation\n","\n","Bayesian last layer is attractive when full BNN inference is too expensive but an uncertainty-aware sequential optimizer is still needed. Its limitation is structural: uncertainty in the learned feature representation is omitted, so OOD confidence can be misleading.\n"]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.x"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}